      "content": [
        {
          "type": "toolResponse",
          "id": "call_03_GtVLSxnMf7BXIwMidrOU9085",
          "toolResult": {
            "status": "success",
            "value": {
              "resultType": "complete",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "# Loaded: lore-project-index/references/saas-wedges.md\n\n# SaaS wedges\n\nDecided 2026-09-02, director seat. Wedge 1 has its own entry at `lore-project-attested-bundles`. This is the other eleven and the frame that ranked them.\n\n## The envelope, after six corrections\n\nSix of nine opening propositions were wrong and Kai overturned all six. The corrected frame is what the ranking rests on.\n\n* **Build throughput is not the constraint.** Four headlines in 112 days, so buildability is not a scoring axis.\n* **Killing work is an asset, not a risk.** The archive rate is high and deliberate, so every wedge carries an exit condition because she acts on them.\n* **On-call is a moat.** The disdain is for a pager serving goals she does not share. Reliability-shaped products get more attractive, not less.\n* **Only the ADU is closed to outside money.** Company financing form is open and follows the product. Self-funded promo spend is priced in ADU-months.\n* **The steady-state bar is a ceiling test on a ten-year horizon**, not a hurdle rate. The figure derives from the independent rate in `lore-self-compensation` and is not restated here. A low ceiling is fatal. A slow start is not.\n* **Reach was measured and is not uniformly small.** LinkedIn converts far better per post than Bluesky and reaches past the follower graph, into a majority software-development, heavily senior audience. Figures in `lore-self-current-life-context`.\n\n## The endorsed four\n\nRanked 1 to 4, filed as `teable:coilyco-flight-deck/housecast#6815`, `teable:coilyco-gaming/sirens-echo#6816`, `teable:coilyco-flight-deck/umbra#6817`, `teable:coilyco-flight-deck/mcp-beaver#6818`.\n\n**Three of the four are one bet.** Attested bundles, refusal traces and the guarded MCP endpoint all need the agent market to keep deepening. The documentation deficit needs only that communities ask questions their docs cannot answer, which was true in 2010. The set is less diversified than four items suggests, and what diversification exists is bought entirely by the lowest-ceiling member.\n\n**Wedge 4 dropped hardest on research.** Kong AI Gateway 3.13 shipped MCP Tool ACLs: declarative YAML, default-deny. Red Hat, Cerbos, ToolHive and Permit.io are all in it, thirteen named gateways. **Close it as a product, keep mcp-beaver as infrastructure.** So the endorsed set is three live and one closed, and `teable:coilyco-flight-deck/mcp-beaver#6818` still reads as a wedge-4 proving slice, which is the row outliving the decision rather than a second opinion about it.\n\n## The five held\n\nAgent incident response, competitive subjective evals, covered-AI provenance evidence, judgement packs, game community server ops. Real, not started. Covered-AI has the highest ceiling in the set and the worst fit for evenings.\n\n## The three closed, with reopen conditions\n\n* **Harness conformance testing.** Genuinely novel, genuinely early. **Reopens when Kai can name two teams running two harnesses in production who are paying attention to the difference.** Not two who could.\n* **Per-role model spend attribution.** The defect is too thin, since Helicone and Langfuse attribute by key and adding a role dimension is a sprint. **Reopens if the demand turns out to be role-level budget enforcement rather than reporting.**\n* **Personal relationship memory.** Consumer acquisition costs and a ceiling well under the bar. **Closed as a business and recommended as personal infrastructure**, because it services the warm-connection channel every other wedge depends on.\n\n## Sequencing\n\n**Superseded 2026-09-03. Kai went all in on wedge 1**, which grew a vertical and a services layer in `lore-project-attested-bundles`. Wedge 2 is no longer first and no longer gates wedge 1. The retired order was wedge 2 for one week, then wedge 1 behind it.\n\n**The September investment boundary still holds.** All-in names the lane rather than the start date, and nothing new begins before the September speaking obligation ships. Warm introductions are one-shot and get spent on something already running.\n\nRelated: `lore-project-attested-bundles`, `lore-self-business-disposition`.\n\n\n---\nFile loaded into context."
                }
              ],
              "isError": false
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "userVisible": true,
        "agentVisible": true
      }
