                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "# Loaded: lore-self-household-index/references/homestead-findings.md\n\n# household plan, the findings\n\nWhat the plan established, as distinct from its settings\n(`lore-self-homestead-threshold`), its salary lock\n(`lore-self-homestead-salary-lock`) and its supplied inputs\n(`lore-self-homestead-inputs`). These move on a re-run rather than on a new\nnumber arriving.\n\n**Sharing is worth more than the sum shared.** At $175/hr, shared gives $4,949k and zero penalties. Separate gives $3,864k, $329k of penalties, and the other ledger dry in 2051. Under sharing **who pays for which child makes no difference**, so that conversation only exists where money is kept apart.\n\n**The share ramp matches a real career shape. Utilisation is the fragile part.** Blending wage and independent work is hybrid entrepreneurship, a studied path, and self-employment rises with age from about 8% of workers aged 25-49 to 24% at 65+. Volatility, which the ramp ignores, does not matter: at 35% unbiased noise, no run in 2000 exhausts the balance. **Persistent shortfall is what kills it**, about $855k per 10% below plan, so the exposed term is utilisation, worth $1.9M between 70% and 55%. The break-even rate against $200k is $137/hr at 70%, recomputed 2026-09-13; the recorded $185/hr at 65% was against the superseded $250k. Evidence: `teable:coilyco-bridge/lore#7633`.\n\n**Whether the ramp is preference or forecast is unresolved, and Kai says both.** Self-employment rises with age partly because the employed market deteriorates (`teable:coilyco-bridge/inbox#7616`). As preference the schedule is a plan. As forecast, holding 25% employed income at 67 is the optimistic assumption, not the conservative one.\n\n**Her income stops dead at 45, the sharpest edge in the plan.** Net flow runs about $156,000 a year to 2032 and $2,836 in 2033, a fall of $153,008 in one step, because her salary and the coverage it funds end in the same year.\n\n**No realistic university cost threatens the plan.** The break-even is about $227,276 a child-year, four times the dearest real option, and even a private sticker clears $4.0M at 2082.\n\n**Establishing that her salary covers the household was worth $4.03M**, more than the whole salary lock cost. It moved the spend headroom from $10,180 a year to $37,716, which is what stopped university deciding the plan.\n\n**Everything is earned before 2032.** The balance peaks near $5.84M in 2059, then draws $185,000 a year against a 3% return that nearly offsets it. The trough is still 2026.\n\n**Each year the metamour works is worth about $20k a year of Kai's income, permanently.** At 48 no promotion is needed, at 45 it is load-bearing, at 42 the plan fails whatever Kai earns.\n\n**Kai and Zulu never fail** in any configuration tested. Every failure lands on the person with no earnings record and on her child.\n\n## What stays unmodelled\n\nNo disability, unemployment or public assistance income. Returns deterministic,\nno variance. The independent-share schedule is a plausible path rather than a\nprediction and does real work in the numbers. Land tenure out of scope by Kai's\ndirection.\n\n## What stays unmodelled\n\nNo disability, unemployment or public assistance income. Returns deterministic,\nno variance. The independent-share schedule is a plausible path rather than a\nprediction and does real work in the numbers. Land tenure out of scope by Kai's\ndirection.\n\n## Wall\n\n**Category 1 on `lore-rule-disclosure-gradient`**, because this records another\nadult's finances and her exit age, which is not Kai's to spend. No bio, cover\nnote, recruiter reply, post, or public tracker.\n\n\n---\nFile loaded into context."
                }
