pstream inference on this. The Jev instructions say \"Interactive decisions only, bulk p...\" and \"Jev takes no images and answers only the typed shape it was asked.\"\n\nI think the guardrail-consistent answer is: use Jev for the verdict. Let me do it. But I should also be efficient — one Jev call with a couple of noul questions (umbra buyer? acompose buyer?) rather than three separate calls.\n\nActually, the create_noul_decision schema takes `questions` as a map (object) where each value is a noul question. So I can put multiple noul questions in one call. Let me structure:\n\nmodel: \"jev-latest\"\nstate: compact object describing the situation.\nquestions: {\n  \"umbra_buyer\": { type: \"noul\", instructions: \"...\", criteria: { true: \"...\", false: \"...\" } },\n  \"acompose_buyer\": { type: \"noul\", instructions: \"...\", criteria: { true: \"...\", false: \"...\" } }\n}\n\nWait, the noul criteria schema: `criteria` has `true` and `false` strings. These describe what \"yes\" and \"no\" mean.\n\nLet me look at the schema again precisely:\n\ncreate_noul_decision:\n- model: string\n- questions: object, additionalProperties → anyOf [ {criteria: {true, false}, instructions, type: \"noul\"} ]\n- state: object\n\nSo questions is a map of name → noul question object with instructions, type, criteria{true,false}.\n\ncreate_score_decision:\n- model, questions map → score object {criteria: array (min 2 max 10 items), instructions, type \"score\"}, state.\n\ncreate_choice_decision:\n- model, questions map → choice object {criteria: object, instructions, type \"choice\"}, state.\n\nOK. So I can do a noul for the buyer question, or a score for \"likelihood a buyer exists.\"\n\nLet me think about what's most decision-useful and guardrail-aligned. The user asked \"say whether anyone would actually buy one.\" That's a noul. But a more informative verdict would be a score (ordered level) of likelihood. The tool doc says \"score is an ordered level.\"\n\nI'll do a score for \"likelihood that within 12 months a paying buyer exists for a custom cut + support\" for umbra, and a noul for acompose (whether it's even buyable as a standalone custom cut given it depends on housecast). Actually, maybe simpler: two nouls.\n\nHmm, let me not overcomplicate. Let me do:\n\n1. A noul decision: \"Would anyone actually buy a custom one-time cut + long-term support of umbra?\" (yes/no)\n2. A noul decision: \"Would anyone actually buy a custom one-time cut + long-term support of acompose?\" (yes/no)\n\nBoth in one call, one state.\n\nActually, I realize I should think about whether the \"state\" is meant to be the full situation. Let me write a concise state object.\n\nLet me also reconsider: is calling Jev going to work? The MCP is \"kai-server_30089_mcp\" and it's active in my tools. The instructions in the system prompt describe \"kai-server_30089_mcp\" as \"This server exposes only policy-approved tools... Ask Jev (TypeSafe System One) a typed decision question through Agent Proxy.\" And separately there's \"tailnet_coilyco_jev\" listed as a skill.\n\nSo I have the tools. Let me use them. This honors the guardrail \"verdict from a separate decision model.\"\n\nLet me draft the Jev state and questions.\n\nState (compact, factual, no comp invention):\n- umbra: Kai's open-source agent-permission/occlusion engine (argv validation, scope tokens, per-invocation egress proxy, audit log, exit-code taxonomy). Successor to cli-guard. A headline in her portfolio. No customers, no buyer-facing artifact; current surfaces (code, talks, streams) reach practitioners not buyers.\n- acompose (agent-compose): renders a housecast roster bundle into harness surfaces (Claude Code, Codex, Goose, OpenCode) as named specialists. Depends on housecast upstream. No customers.\n- Confirmed pricing anchor: $150/hr rule rate at 70% utilisation. Household break-even $137/hr at 70%. No premium tier, walk-away, or ladder confirmed.\n- The proposed offer shape: custom one-time cut (scoped build/integration) + recurring long-term support retainer.\n- The offer shape itself is not a confirmed offering; it's being evaluated.\n\nQuestions:\n\nnoul \"umbra_buyer_12mo\":\ninstructions: \"Within the next 12 months, is there a real buyer who would pay Kai for a custom one-time cut plus long-term support of umbra (agent permission/occlusion enforcement), given she currently has no customers, no buyer-facing sales artifact, and her surfaces reach practitioners rather than technical buyers?\"\ncriteria:\n  true: \"Yes — at least one genuine buyer with a budget is likely to pay for this within 12 months.\"\n  false: \"No — there is no near-term evidence of a paying buyer for this within 12 months.\"\n\nnoul \"acompose_buyer_12mo\":\ninstructions: \"Within the next 12 months, is there a real buyer who would pay Kai for a custom one-time cut plus long-term support of acompose (rendering a housecast roster into named harness specialists), given it depends on the housecast roster engine upstream and she has no customers or buyer-facing artifact?\"\ncriteria:\n  true: \"Yes — at least one genuine buyer with a budget is likely to pay for this within 12 months.\"\n  false: \"No — there is no near-term evidence of a paying buyer for this within 12 months.\"\n\nHmm wait, the noul criteria schema is `criteria: {properties: {false, true}}` — actually it says `criteria: {\"properties\": {\"false\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"true\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"type\": \"object\", \"required\": []}`. So criteria is an object with \"true\" and \"false\" string keys. I provide {\"true\": \"...\", \"false\": \"...\"}.\n\nModel: \"jev-latest\".\n\nLet me write this call. Also, I should consider a score for \"price band ceiling\" — but the guardrail says a number I produce is a defect; the price bands should come from... hmm. Actually the user wants price bands from me. The confirmed rate gives a basis. I'll produce bands as arithmetic on the $150 rate with clearly-flagged hour estimates, and note that the ceiling test (steady-state bar) derives from the independent rate in lore-self-compensation and is \"not restated here\" (saas-wedges says the figure is not restated — so I should NOT restate a steady-state bar number; there isn't one I can cite beyond $150/hr).\n\nOK. Let me also decide: do I even need to call Jev? Let me weigh. The guardrail is explicit and I'm the director. Calling Jev is the guardrail-conformant act for \"the verdict.\" And it's cheap enough. I'll do it.\n\nBut actually — let me reconsider once more. Is the guardrail really requiring a Jev call for every assessment, or is \"separate decision model\" a conceptual instruction (e.g., use a rubric rather than gut)? The skill says \"the verdict taken from a separate decision model rather than generated here\" and lists \"a number this seat produced on its own\" as a defect. Jev is literally named as the typed-decision model available via MCP. I have the tools. I'll use them — it's the defensible, on-charter move, and it demonstrates the guardrail actually firing rather than just being described.\n\nLet me make the Jev call now. I'll do two noul questions in one create_noul_decision call.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the shape. For \"would anyone buy,\" maybe a single score decision is cleaner than two nouls, because the answer isn't clean yes/no — it's a likelihood. But the user literally asked \"say whether anyone would actually buy one,\" which is yes/no. I'll do noul for each project. Two nouls, one call.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nAfter I get Jev's verdict, I'll compose the final answer.\n\nLet me also prepare my todo. The instructions say \"Once given a task, immediately update your todo.\" I've been loading skills. Let me write a quick todo. Actually I should have done this earlier but let me do it now alongside.\n\nLet me write todo and make the Jev call. These are independent? The todo write and the Jev call are independent. But I want the Jev result before final answer. Let me do todo first, then Jev call (or in parallel). I can do them in parallel since they're independent.\n\nActually, I'll do the Jev call and the todo write in the same block.\n\nLet me draft the state object carefully. The state is \"an object describing the situation the questions are about.\" Keep it factual and compact.\n\nstate = {\n  \"subject\": \"Kai Ase Siren, platform engineer with an open-source agent-safety portfolio\",\n  \"projects\": {\n    \"umbra\": \"agent occlusion/permission engine: argv validation before execve, per-verb scope tokens, per-invocation egress proxy, audit log, published exit-code taxonomy. Successor to cli-guard. Headline portfolio project. No customers.\",\n    \"acompose\": \"renders a housecast roster bundle into named harness specialists (Claude Code, Codex, Goose, OpenCode) with no executable authority. Depends on housecast roster engine upstream. No customers.\"\n  },\n  \"confirmed_pricing\": \"rule rate $150/hr at 70% utilisation; household break-even $137/hr at 70%; no premium tier, walk-away, or negotiation ladder confirmed\",\n  \"offer_shape_under_evaluation\": \"custom one-time cut (scoped build/integration) plus recurring long-term support retainer\",\n  \"current_reach\": \"surfaces (code, talks, live streams) reach practitioners/workers, not technical buyers; no buyer-facing sales artifact naming the buyer's problem and cost of inaction\"\n}\n\nGood.\n\nNow the questions. Let me write concise but complete instructions.\n\nLet me go.\n\nActually, one more consideration: should I include the price bands in the Jev state so Jev can opine on whether the bands are realistic? The user asked for price bands AND \"would anyone buy.\" The \"would anyone buy\" is the verdict question. The price bands I'll produce as inference. I could add a score question on ceiling but that risks inventing numbers through Jev too. Keep it to the buy/no-buy noul, which is what the guardrail needs (the verdict).\n\nLet me proceed with the Jev call + todo.\n\nFor the todo, quick: \n- [x] Load pricing/comp/project lore\n- [x] Confirm rate anchors and project definitions\n- [ ] Route buyer verdict through Jev\n- [ ] Produce price bands (flagged as inference) + buy/don't-buy verdict\n\nLet me write it.",
